# Shreder access file (optional). Put it at /root/shreder.key on FRA, mode 600 (sudo install -m 600 ...).
# Without this file the recorder uses the built-in default endpoint with IP-allowlist auth (no token),
# which is what the trial uses (FRA 84.32.100.36 allowlisted). Values are never printed; logs show an endpoint id.
#
# endpoint = http://fra-allnodes.binary.shreder.xyz:9991     # or https://... ; host:port alone means http://
# token = <only if Shreder issues one>
# header = x-token                                           # metadata key for the token (e.g. authorization + token "Bearer ...")
#
# Bare lines also work: a line that looks like a URL/host:port is the endpoint, any other line is the token.
